One component, two SW items (2026-09-01).  MIMXRT1062.h line 280 includes
core_cm7.h, so vendoring the MCUX SDK device layer (firmware/vendor/mcux_sdk/,
OI-SWCI-20) needed CMSIS-Core(M) for Cortex-M7 as well as for Cortex-M0+.  The
alternative was a second copy of cmsis_version.h, cmsis_compiler.h, cmsis_gcc.h
and mpu_armv7.h inside the MCUX directory.  Two byte-identical copies of one SOUP
component is worse than one copy serving two SW items: it doubles the surface to
justify, and it makes a future tag bump a change that can be applied to one copy
and not the other.  The core headers themselves are disjoint — core_cm0plus.h is
included only by stm32g071xx.h (SW-01) and core_cm7.h only by MIMXRT1062.h
(SW-02) — and the two builds are separate CMake projects with separate toolchain
files, so neither can reach the other's core header by accident.

