Why each file is here — none is aspirational:
  core_cm0plus.h    included unconditionally by stm32g071xx.h line 115.  There is
                    no way to use the ST device header without it.
  cmsis_version.h   included by core_cm0plus.h line 63.
  cmsis_compiler.h  included by core_cm0plus.h line 115.
  cmsis_gcc.h       selected by cmsis_compiler.h line 54 for __GNUC__ builds.
  mpu_armv7.h       included by core_cm0plus.h line 1007 because stm32g071xx.h
                    sets __MPU_PRESENT 1U.  Verified by deletion: removing this
                    file fails the compile with "mpu_armv7.h: No such file".
                    NeurOne calls no MPU function; the file is a transitive
                    requirement of the device header, not a feature choice.
                    core_cm7.h includes it for the same reason on the SW-02 side.
  core_cm7.h        included unconditionally by MIMXRT1062.h line 280.  There is
                    no way to use the MCUX device header without it.
  cachel1_armv7.h   included by core_cm7.h line 2234 because the RT1062 has L1
                    caches (__DCACHE_PRESENT / __ICACHE_PRESENT).  Verified by
                    deletion: removing it fails the compile of
                    system_MIMXRT1062.c with "cachel1_armv7.h: No such file".
                    SystemInit() line 128 calls SCB_EnableICache() from this
                    header under #if __ICACHE_PRESENT, so unlike mpu_armv7.h it
                    is not merely a transitive include — it is called.  (The
                    D-cache half is NOT enabled by SystemInit; nothing in-tree
                    calls SCB_EnableDCache.)

